# Code owners for this repository (issue #142).
#
# CODEOWNERS on its own does not require anything: it names who is requested for
# review. It becomes an enforced control only when `main`'s branch protection
# turns on "require review from Code Owners", which is a repository setting and
# is tracked separately in ADR 0018. This file is the in-repo half of that
# control, and is inert until the setting is enabled.
#
# That setting is currently OFF, deliberately. Scorecard's tier 4 needs code-owner
# review AND two approving reviews; with a single active maintainer the second is
# unobtainable, so enabling code-owner review scored nothing while costing an
# override on every merge. This file stays committed so turning it on is a
# one-line change once a second maintainer makes that tier reachable.
#
# Ordering matters: the LAST matching pattern wins, so the catch-all comes first
# and the security-sensitive paths that follow deliberately override it.

# Everything, unless a more specific rule below claims it.
